#
# Conformance case: teleology/iteration-combinator.
#
# A logic:Iteration is EXECUTED under executional entailment: its logic:iterationCondition (resourceStillAvailable) holds at the start, so the body (retryAction) runs ONE pass — deleting resourceStillAvailable (supersession) and asserting retryComplete — after which the condition no longer holds and the loop terminates. The engine records the executed path and the per-pass supersession substrate. Proves while-condition iteration with a terminating loop.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/iteration-combinator/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
